Z||000000||fropuff||05-30-2000||05:15 PM||||Hey, I was wondering if anyone knows how to take off the molding.  I need to take off the molding off of my 86 GT to get ready for a paint job.  Does anyone know?  I don't want to break any clips if possible, and I want to be as careful as I can.  <P>P.S.  Also, I am looking for the rear piece of molding for my GT.  It is the rounded piece with the GT lettering on the right hand side.  It goes under the tail lamps, over the rear bumper.  Does anyone have one?  Thanks.||||reg||10
Z||000001||sluppy123||05-30-2000||06:36 PM||||Good luck getting the clips out of the slots without breaking them,  I used a screw driver to bend the center tab down and slide the clip out, but i broke everyone of them off. the little piece behind the door handle is held on by a nut from the back, and the little pointed pieces on the nose are held on with nuts also.  <P>Replacement clips are available from GM part # 12337975 .86 cents apiece<P>-Brian<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fret Naught||05-30-2000||06:53 PM||||Yeah what he said, buy the clips, cause they are going to break, just been there and done that!!!||||reg||7
Z||000003||fropuff||05-30-2000||08:49 PM||||How many clips in total are there?  I should also buy some extras in case there is a break of one or two.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||cobra427||05-30-2000||11:53 PM||||fropuf,<BR>that rear piece of molding in the back, if I'm not mistaken, is part of the rear clip. They are all one piece. It is just painted black||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||05-31-2000||07:39 AM||||correct... at least on the GT cars, it is part of the bumper.<P>the clips are also available from the fiero store.  i just ordered a set for both Qtr panels.<P>they also have the rivets that are used to attach the body work of the car.  i had been haveing a awfull time finding those.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fieroshop||05-31-2000||10:42 AM||||I have all those clips and rivets both in plastic and in aluminum.||||reg||1
